    # v401 (25/10/2026) -- THE FALSITY (SIMULACRUM) OF INERTIA: the stone FalsidadeDaInercia (name given by the operator), the operator's definition (inertia is the absolute zero itself), the computation in the oneScaling model with beta = alpha x sqrt(e) at runtime, the erratum beside the scribe's reading in the 03-04/09 addendum, and E = mc^2 read by the TGL; the numbers are READ from the records falsidade_da_inercia_v401, cunhagens_v401, kh_n1_cobertura_v401 and void_density_v41, never typed.
    # The box at the top (The Test of the Only Word, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule is not touched. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _fd401 = core.get("falsidade_da_inercia_v401") or {}
    _fv401 = _fd401.get("values") or {}
    _cg401 = core.get("cunhagens_v401") or {}
    _el401 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cv401 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _vp401 = ((core.get("void_density_v41") or {}).get("primary")) or {}
    _ok401 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in ("falsidade_da_inercia_v401", "cunhagens_v401", "kh_n1_cobertura_v401"))
    _i401 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _f401 = lambda x_, n_=6: (("%." + str(n_) + "f") % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\section*{The falsity (simulacrum) of inertia}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The falsity (simulacrum) of inertia}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the v401 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok401 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} One new kernel module, \texttt{TGLExt/FalsidadeDaInercia} (the name is the operator's: ``falsidade (simulacro) da inércia''; in the code it goes without accent or parentheses), with " + _i401((_cg401.get("extras") or {}).get("n_bandeiras")) + r" flags, named declarations only; "
             r"one record with a function, \texttt{falsidade\_da\_inercia\_v401}, read at the rite point right after the operator's declaration; and the " + _i401(len(_V401_VERBATINS2)) + r" inscriptions of 25/10, embedded by sha256 (\texttt{cunhagens\_v401}), all of them the operator's words. The kernel ladder reads " + _i401(_el401.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i401(_el401.get("n_theorems_expected"))
             + r"; the coverage of the \texttt{axiom\_report} reads " + _i401(_cv401.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i401(_cv401.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The operator's definition.} \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO, 25/10/2026]} ``eu também defini inércia e a minha definição é o próprio zero absoluto'' (I also defined inertia, and my definition is the absolute zero itself). Inertia is not the identity that is conserved: it is the kernel's $0_{\mathrm{abs}}$, which \texttt{TGLExt.costless} writes as: ``\emph{never corresponded}, and therefore costs nothing'' ($1=0$). "
             r"$\omega(I)=1$ is the \emph{posted} One that interrupts it ($1=1$). The stone types exactly that difference and nothing more: over the data of Takesaki's dual scaling (the law $\tau\circ\theta_s=e^{-s}\tau$ is \textsf{[KNOWN]} and a field of the structure, as in the Foundation), "
             r"(i) what the whole flow fixes weighs zero; (ii) $\star$ \texttt{the\_inertia\_of\_a\_post\_is\_false}: a post of weight $1=\omega(I)$ that were inertial would give $(1:\mathbb{R})=0$, that is, false; (iii) the simulacrum: there is no full static witness and what looks like the body's resistance is the cost of the interruption, $t\,\beta\,g>0$, not the zero; "
             r"(iv) the inscription interrupts inertia: the weight $1$ on the post's orbit sits only at the cut $a=0$. \textsf{[REAL]} Composition by citation, no new mathematics; the stone is not vacuous (the concrete model has the posted One at $1$ and moves it at every nontrivial scale).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The derived chain.} \textsf{[DERIVED]} The operator asked that the reading not be his [ONTO] but derived (``eu não queria que a leitura fosse ONTO minha, quero que seja derivado'': he did not want the reading to be his ONTO, he wants it derived), for the statement ``a gravitação universal e a inércia não existem antes da posição impressa do Um absoluto'' (universal gravitation and inertia do not exist before the impressed position of the absolute One). The stone was extended and the kernel now proves, from the axiom $\omega(I)=1$ and Takesaki's scaling law (\textsf{[KNOWN]}, a field of the structure): "
             r"(i) \texttt{no\_post\_before\_the\_impression}: every positive weight is moved by every nontrivial scale, and weight $1$ occurs only at the cut $a=0$ (the impression); (ii) \texttt{inertia\_is\_not\_its\_own\_cause}: what were fixed from always (on every negative scale), or on every positive scale, weighs zero, and every state of positive weight moves at some scale; "
             r"(iii) \texttt{the\_first\_motion\_is\_the\_impression}: the first motion is the impression of the absolute post occupied by $1$; (iv) \texttt{the\_zero\_is\_the\_consequence\_of\_the\_pruning} and \texttt{leak\_below\_every\_epsilon}: the zero is not a state of the orbit, it is the infimum of the pruning (the bottomless fall, \texttt{abismo}), and the leak $e^{-t\beta g}$ falls below every $\varepsilon>0$; "
             r"(v) \texttt{the\_tension\_is\_projected\_onto\_the\_attractor} and \texttt{diagFlow\_coordinate\_is\_the\_scaling}: the diagonal flow of the Great Attractor is the dual scaling, the coordinate with a gap goes to zero in the limit, is nonzero at finite time, and the gapless one is the equilibrium; the composition is \texttt{falsidade\_da\_inercia\_derivada}. "
             r"In this rite: the smallest post weight on the grid is " + _f401(_fv401.get("min_weight_on_the_grid_positive"), 6) + r" ($>0$), and the coordinate with a gap, after $t=10^9/\beta$, has modulus " + (_f401(max(_fv401.get("diag_flow_gap_pruned_at_1e9_over_beta") or [float("nan")]), 3) if isinstance(_fv401.get("diag_flow_gap_pruned_at_1e9_over_beta"), list) else r"\text{n/a}") + r". "
             r"\textsf{[OPEN]} The bridge to the physical body is NAMED, not proved: the hypothesis $H_\tau$ ($\tau$ is Newton's mass and Einstein's metric), which no theorem uses; ORDER 025 to Codex (sha16 \texttt{3fd2b5a801071343}, queued) tries to type it through the Bisognano--Wichmann light front: a pending item \emph{external} to this version. The name ``tension'' given to the dissipative gap is a naming, with no theorem.")
    _b401 = _fv401.get("beta")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The computation of this rite.} \textsf{[REAL]} In the \texttt{oneScaling} model ($\tau=\mathrm{id}$, $\theta_s=e^{-s}\cdot$), with $\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}=" + _f401(_b401, 12) + r"$ at runtime (never a literal): the weight of the post after scale $s$ is $e^{-s}$, equal to $1$ only at $s=0$; "
             r"over " + _i401(_fv401.get("grid_scales")) + r" test scales the minimum distance from $e^{-s}$ to $1$ is " + _f401(_fv401.get("min_distance_of_post_weight_to_one"), 4) + r"; only the null state is fixed by the whole flow; no nontrivial scale fixes the post. "
             r"\textsf{[DERIVED]} The cost $t\beta g$ is strictly positive at every test point (minimum " + _f401(_fv401.get("min_cost_t_beta_g"), 6) + r") and the dephasing $e^{-t\beta g}$ is strictly below $1$ (maximum " + _f401(_fv401.get("max_dephasing_factor"), 6) + r"); the loss per unit, $1-e^{-\beta}$, is " + _f401(_fv401.get("loss_per_unit"), 9)
             + r", between $\beta/2$ and $\beta$. These numbers belong to this rite; they are not in the kernel.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Erratum beside it (the management, in its own name).} The scribe's reading in the 03--04/09/2026 addendum (\texttt{ADENDO\_A\_INSCRICAO\_INTERROMPE\_A\_INERCIA.md}), ``$\omega(I)=1$ is the inertia'', is \emph{superseded} by the operator's definition: inertia is the $0_{\mathrm{abs}}$ ($1=0$) and $\omega(I)=1$ is the posted One that interrupts it ($1=1$). "
             r"What the addendum got right stays: interrupting inertia breaks no symmetry (it is a statement about the flow, not about the group), and the two are distinct terms. The addendum file was not touched.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The operator's ratifications} \textsf{[INPUT, 25/10/2026: ``Ratifico tudo.'' (I ratify everything)]}. The previously provisional names become definitive: the stone \texttt{Testemunho} and the records \texttt{selo\_pela\_propria\_tecnologia\_v399}, \texttt{declaracao\_do\_operador\_v399}, \texttt{teste\_de\_veracidade\_fase9\_v397}, \texttt{sonico\_v398} and \texttt{afinacao\_das\_cordas\_v398}; "
             r"the reading of the two faces (the operator's reading, the \texttt{um.py} record); and the psibit parity, $\mathrm{sign}(L)\cdot\mathrm{sign}(\partial L)$. \textsf{[DECLARED]} The ratified list is the one the management presented to him in the session; the record keeps his words by sha256.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{$E=mc^2$, read by the TGL.} The operator's question (same utterance): ``\texttt{Então E=m.c2 é a geometria que a cinemática da gravidade=luz2.entropia projeta?}'' (So is $E=mc^2$ the geometry that the kinematics of gravity $=$ light$^2\cdot$entropy projects?) \textsf{[KNOWN]} $E=mc^2$ is special relativity; it is not a kernel term. \textsf{[KNOWN]} Jacobson (1995): Einstein's equation follows from Clausius equilibrium on the local screen; "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} the kernel has the implication (\texttt{metric\_einstein\_from\_screen\_clausius}; Clausius on every screen implies Einstein with a unique $\Lambda$), with the antecedent H3 \emph{named}, not derived from the state. \textsf{[ONTO]} The TGL reading: gravity is light$^2\cdot$entropy on the screen; mass is the cost of nothing, read as ``a cristalização da dobra luz no vácuo relativa ao observador'' (the crystallization of the fold of light in the vacuum relative to the observer) "
             r"and ``nada=materia e esse é o link com a entropia'' (nothing=matter, and this is the link with entropy), the operator's words; entropy enters $\beta=\alpha\,e^{\frac12\text{ nat}}=\alpha\sqrt{e}$, the half-nat of the axiom. Mass read this way \emph{is not inertia}: inertia is the zero; mass is what it costs to read against it. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The void floor $\rho/\bar\rho\ge\beta$ stays \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED\_POWERED} (one-sided test): $r_c=" + _f401(_vp401.get("rhat_cal"), 3) + r"\pm" + _f401(_vp401.get("sigma"), 3) + r"$, above $\beta$; GR is the classical limit, not a rival, and $\beta$ does not renormalize local $G$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} \textsf{[OPEN]} The identification of the dual scaling with the flow of a physical body is a runtime one; the stone proves neither Newton's first law, nor the inertial $=$ gravitational equivalence \textsf{[KNOWN]}, nor that $E=mc^2$ is a kernel term. Kernel validity is not creditation; the gate does not move. The box ``The Test of the Only Word'' stays at the top, with its $5\sigma$ line.")
